# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PREMIA trading section (additive, feature-flagged, OPT-IN).
#
# PREMIA IS OFF UNLESS YOU TURN IT ON. Exactly one var is required —
# VITE_FEATURE_PREMIA="true". Everything else (Base-mainnet addresses, live
# mode, RPCs, faucet size) already has a working default in
# src/v2/lib/premia/config.ts, so set the rest only to override.
#
# WHY OPT-IN: the beta is collateralised by prmUSD, a mock ERC-20 with an open
# faucet and NO monetary value, and the mark still runs on the placeholder
# λ_ref curve rather than the calibrated M^ref table. A production deployment
# must decide to expose that deliberately — it must never arrive by default.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Feature flag (REQUIRED to show the section). "true" or "1" = on; anything
# else, or unset, = off: the routes and the Markets nav item never register.
#
# NOTE: this is only the BUILD-LEVEL kill switch. PREMIA is also invite-only
# at runtime: the nav item, the mobile tab and the routes additionally require
# `hasAccess` from GET /v1/premia/beta/status, which a user obtains by
# redeeming an invite at /beta/<code>. The flag alone does not grant access,
# and the status check fails closed, so an unreachable backend admits nobody.
# app-lp/.env sets this to "true" for local development.
# PRODUCTION (Vercel etc.): leave this UNSET to keep PREMIA off, or set it
# explicitly to "true" when you intend to expose the beta.
VITE_FEATURE_PREMIA=true

# Mode: "live" (default — contract reads + sponsored user-ops through the Rift
# wallet) or "mock" (in-browser mock, nothing hits chain).
# VITE_PREMIA_MODE=mock

# Base RPC. First URL wins; the rest are automatic fallbacks. Defaults to
# base-rpc.publicnode.com → base.drpc.org → mainnet.base.org.
# DO NOT use base.llamarpc.com: it returns 525s and falsely reports the
# deployed contracts as having no code.
# VITE_PREMIA_RPC_URL=https://base-rpc.publicnode.com
# VITE_PREMIA_RPC_URLS=https://base-rpc.publicnode.com,https://base.drpc.org

# ── Deployed PREMIA contracts on Base mainnet (chainId 8453) ──────────────
# These are the defaults in config.ts; listed here for reference/override.
# VITE_PREMIA_PRMUSD=0x7152280AfE7493d84533565Cd5c79B5d4B4EC4CB
# VITE_PREMIA_VAULT=0x127048434EfD4ac79e5E4ff41E1c6e3d5Fd0279A
# VITE_PREMIA_FACTORY=0xf9CFf47DE2E6bEAA5F32Cf2090E35aC3B829c3A8
# VITE_PREMIA_ORACLE=0x93D1dbAC87AcCf85C3070eEdD9EeD0Ad699b7090
# VITE_PREMIA_FEE_SPLITTER=0x17CA473D42131CB27C1BA129A4404a2FF0140f81
# VITE_PREMIA_KEEPER=0xA10042C12F0ADE1CAF928F023799F6F594C4236b

# ── Per-market wiring ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each market's PerpMarket ADDRESS is resolved at runtime from
# MarketFactory.marketOf(marketId); set the _MARKET_ var only to pin it and
# skip that read. Both markets below are deployed on Base mainnet.
#
# Flagship — NGN·USDT street premium. keccak256("PREMIA.NG.USDT.PREMIUM.V1").
# VITE_PREMIA_MARKETID_NGN=0x073b4c4094438f226383e78329ff6ff51bea64fc33fc05785a8b5e7555556338
# VITE_PREMIA_MARKET_NGN=0xa2F5e7CE731b1ed1e7bc0501eAEF451685AA3dE7
#
# The diesel-in-naira energy market is deployed and Frozen on chain but is
# DELISTED from the UI (2026-11-23) pending an economics redesign. Do not
# re-add it here without re-adding it to markets.ts.

# Lower bound for the eth_getLogs scans that build real fill history (cost
# basis / P&L) and the oracle's own index history (the chart).
# VITE_PREMIA_DEPLOY_BLOCK=60887800

# prmUSD faucet drip size, whole prmUSD. The contract mints 10,000 per call
# with a 24h per-address cooldown — only change this if the token changes.
# VITE_PREMIA_FAUCET_AMOUNT=10000

# Slippage bound applied to the mark quoted by PerpMarket.quote(), percent.
# VITE_PREMIA_SLIPPAGE_PCT=1

# NOTE: collateral is prmUSD — a 6-decimal TEST token with no value. Gas is
# sponsored and paid in USDC via the Rift paymaster (lib/nonCustodial.ts
# `sendChainTx`), the same path app-lp's swap already uses. There is no
# WalletConnect step: the signed-in in-app wallet signs every user-op.
